<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter von Biron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1724–1800</span> · Also known as Peter, Duke of Courland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter von Biron was the last Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> and Semigallia, ruling from 1769 to 1795. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernst-johann-von-biron">Ernst Johann von Biron</a>, he quarrelled constantly with the Courland nobility. In 1786 he bought the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Sagan</a> in Silesia. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-partition-of-poland">Third Partition of Poland</a> he ceded Courland to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1795 in return for a pension, and he died at Gellenau in Silesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-von-biron.jpg" alt="Peter von Biron" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Hartmann Barisien · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_von_Biron.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
